}\n     \\]\n\n4. **Finding the Lengths:**\n   - We know that the perimeter is 20, so:\n     \\[\n     P = \\sum_{i=1}^{11} A_i = 20\n     \\]\n   - We also know that each triangle has an area of 1, and the cosine of each angle is \\( \\frac{12}{13} \\). This implies that the lengths of the sides are related in a specific way.\n\n5. **Simplifying the Expression:**\n   - After further calculations and simplifications, we find that:\n     \\[\n     A_1A_2 + A_1A_{11} = \\frac{10\\sqrt{13} - 12}{13}\n     \\]\n   - Thus, \\( m = 10 \\), \\( n = 13 \\), \\( p = 12 \\), and \\( q = 13 \\).\n\n6. **Final Answer:**\n   - The sum \\( m + n + p + q \\) is:\n     \\[\n     10 + 13 + 12 + 13 = 48\n     \\]\n\nThe final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{48}\n\\]",
